"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15th, 2023. The project has received a $2M budget approval and is progressing through various phases, including design, development, and testing. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase using AI algorithms. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Upcoming events include a meeting on August 5th to discuss findings, a budget discussion on August 1st, an onboarding session for new members on September 10th, a celebration of the testing milestone on October 10th, and the start of the development phase next month under lead developer Omar Jensen."
